#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0581 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: None of TRTP, TRTPGy, TRTA, and TRTAGy are present and none of the character treatment variables in ADSL defined in the IG are present
#note "G4 skip pin: the rule's wildcard variables match no fixture column (WildcardExpander NoMatch), so the rule does not apply and the harness reports a skip - the scenario pins that boundary until engine gap G4 lands."
# ENGINE-GAP G4 (adam-rule-engine-gaps.md): the universal-absence case (NO treatment
# variable present) cannot be expressed — a wildcard not_exists is skipped when zero
# columns match (WildcardExpander.expand empty -> the rule is skipped), which is exactly
# the violation case. Even with TRTP present the expander matches nothing, so the rule
# never executes on this fixture - hence the expect=skipped pin. The invalid sibling
# (CDISC-AD0581-invalid-ADLBC.cdt) was REMOVED because it cannot fire until G4 lands.
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL type=Num
col TRTP type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 12.5 | Placebo
---
